          "message": "fix: accept Arch Linux packages with non-zero epoch (#14629)\n\n`PKGBUILD.pkgver` and `.PKGINFO.pkgver` are distinct variables with different semantics and naming rules. It is not correct to reject `.PKGINFO.pkgver` because of presence of single `:`.\n\nCo-authored-by: sarge <ephemeralsarge@example.com>\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14629\nReviewed-by: Mathieu Fenniak <mathieu@fenniak.net>\nReviewed-by: Robert Wolff <mahlzahn@posteo.de>\n",
