          "committer": {
            "name": "0ko",
            "email": "redacted@example.invalid",
            "date": "2026-10-01T12:55:59+02:00"
          },
          "message": "feat: accessible aria-labels & working commit description toggles w/o JS (#14158)\n\nThis PR does the following:\n- Adds an `aria-label` and corresponding tooltip to commit message body toggle buttons\n- Grants these buttons a visible focus visual (related: #11894)\n- Ports some of these buttons' JS-based actuation to HTML [`details`/`summary`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/details) elements (repo latest-commit, PR conversation commits; the rest require redesign first, see https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14158#issuecomment-23310016)\n- Introduces a new boolean attribute, `data-tooltip-from-label`, which copies the `aria-label` into a tooltip once on page load, allowing no-JS users to get labeled elements without us having to duplicate the value across two separate attributes.\n    - https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14158#issuecomment-22768531, https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14158#issuecomment-23037904\n- Adds e2e tests around each of these changes\n\nThe new focus visual, as seen in Firefox, which before was visually imperceptible:\n![A dotted border highlights the \"toggle commit message\" ellipsis button, indicating that the button has focus.](/attachments/ffe137ee-5a9c-4fdc-b312-6db88fa65630)\n\nAs with #14103, this new focus border could be much improved, but applying the specific suggestions in #11894 (i.e. applying a consistent site-wide well-visible focus outline) is out-of-scope per feedback on #14161. This PR aims to provide *some* visual focus indication for this control, since there currently is *none*. To accomplish this, I've copied the current typical site-wide focus style (as seen on Firefox. Chrome's might be different). However, if a different style for this control is wanted before this PR merges, I can change that here.\n\n## Testing behavior and visual changes manually\nRun a dev server with `make build frontend && make test-e2e-debugserver`\n\nThere is a test repo at `/user2/multiline-commit-messages` that has various situations which the new buttons should handle gracefully. Try the commit body toggles at the following locations:\n- `/user2/multiline-commit-messages` the latest-commit banner\n- `/user2/multiline-commit-messages/commits/branch/main`\n- `/user2/multiline-commit-messages/pulls/1` the commit in the conversation view\n- `/user2/multiline-commit-messages/pulls/1/commits`\n\nThe Status icons and tags should appear in the usual places. Each ellipsis button should display its respective commit's message body, both with and without Javascript enabled (in the case of latest-commit and PR convo commits). Alignment should match Forgejo's current behavior in similar situations.\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14158\nReviewed-by: 0ko <0ko@noreply.codeberg.org>\n",
